{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "label": "Observability overview", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_four_pillars", "label": "The four observability pillars", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Logs answer what happened and in what order, metrics answer the rate or latency right now, tracing answers what one single request did, and management answers whether the system is alive and healthy."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_extensions_are_opt_in", "label": "Observability extensions are opt-in", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Logging is always on - every actor has this.log, writing to the console by default. The other three are extensions that do not run unless you reach for them, so an app that ignores them has no overhead from unused metrics buffers or unstarted trace exporters."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_sink_selection_guide", "label": "Which log sink to use", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Start with OTLP, since one endpoint format reaches a collector and most SaaS platforms; reach for a native sink only where OTLP does not reach - Graylog over GELF, Sentry for grouping, Loki push for explicit label control, syslog for appliances - and use nothing at all for a container platform scraping stdout, since the console sink in json mode is already NDJSON."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_journald_windows_event_log_omitted", "label": "journald and the Windows Event Log are deliberately not shipped", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both are reached by writing NDJSON to stdout and letting the platform collect it, which the console sink already does; a dedicated sink would add a binary protocol for no reach."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_wiring_order", "label": "What to wire up first", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Logs somewhere durable first - cheapest to set up and the first thing anybody asks for after an incident - then metrics with a Prometheus exporter, then health checks because Kubernetes wants those endpoints anyway, and tracing last: it is more involved (exporter configuration, sampling, cost) and gives diminishing returns for simple apps."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_exporters_overview", "label": "Metrics exporters", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The metrics themselves are framework-internal; getting them to a backend uses an exporter - the Prometheus scrape endpoint, or the prom-client bridge if you already use that library."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_devtools_versus_monitoring", "label": "DevTools is a debugger, not a monitoring stack", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The three pillars watch a system from the outside over time; when you want to look inside one right now - the actor tree, the mailboxes, what a single actor has been doing - attach DevTools instead. It is loopback and unauthenticated by default, and off until you reach for it."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_four_pillars", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_extensions_are_opt_in", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_sink_selection_guide", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_journald_windows_event_log_omitted", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_wiring_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_exporters_overview", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_devtools_versus_monitoring", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_extensions_are_opt_in", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_four_pillars", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_wiring_order", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_observability_overview", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_journald_windows_event_log_omitted", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_sink_selection_guide", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_overview_devtools_versus_monitor